        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-mono tracking-tight text-base-content">
          Building resilient systems with zero bloat.
        </h2>

        <p>
          I started programming back in 2017 during my Computer Science degree, experimenting with low-level C and building static web pages with raw HTML and CSS. Over the last 5+ years, I've had the opportunity to build high-scale web products at startups and tech companies, serving millions of users daily.
        </p>

        <p>
          My engineering philosophy centers around <strong>simplicity, speed, and strict accessibility</strong>. I'm a passionate advocate for static-first web architecture (SSG/Jamstack), edge computing (Cloudflare Workers, Vercel Edge), and lean CSS utility systems that don't weigh down the browser with megabytes of JavaScript.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold font-mono text-base-content pt-4">
          Why I Create on YouTube
        </h3>
        <p>
          In 2023, I launched my YouTube channel <strong>{{ site.youtubeChannel.handle }}</strong> to teach concepts I wish were explained simply when I was starting out: edge runtimes, WebSocket architectures, CSS container queries, and clean component systems. Today, the channel has grown to a community of over 45,000 passionate developers worldwide.
        </p>

